From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: firmware: qcom,scm: Add qcom,uefisecapp

Linux uses QSEECOM only on the machines in qcom_scm's allowlist, so
adding a laptop takes a change to the driver. Whether the firmware runs
the UEFI secure application (uefisecapp), which keeps the UEFI
variables, belongs to the board's firmware, and the board's device tree
can say so. Add a boolean for it.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.yaml
index 037d4ad8f..bd855c1b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.yaml
@@ -123,6 +123,13 @@ properties:
       in the debug mode.
     type: boolean
 
+  qcom,uefisecapp:
+    description:
+      Indicates that the firmware runs the UEFI secure application
+      (uefisecapp) behind QSEECOM, which keeps the UEFI variables, and that
+      it has been tested on this board.
+    type: boolean
+
   qcom,dload-mode:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
     items:
-- 
2.47.3

